msgstr ""
"该连接是故意保持打开状态的。如果将其关闭，将迫使客户端进行新的 TCP 和 TLS 握手，这不仅开销大，而且该负载分流机制无法检测到这一过程。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `Retry-After` value is derived from how long the overload has already "
"lasted.\n"
"The application cannot know when an overload will end, but it does know how "
"long the overload has lasted.\n"
"This is used as a proxy: a brief spike is likely over shortly, while an "
"overload that has been going on for minutes is likely to keep going for a "
"while.\n"
"A client rejected 2 seconds into an overload is therefore told to come back "
"in a few seconds, while a client rejected 5 minutes in is told to stay away "
"for longer."
msgstr ""
"`“Retry-After”的` 值取决于过载已持续了多长时间。应用程序无法预知过载何时结束，但可以知道过载已持续了多长时间。 "
"这被用作一种判断依据：短暂的流量激增很可能很快结束，而持续数分钟的过载则很可能还会持续一段时间。因此，在过载开始 2 "
"秒后被拒绝的客户端会被告知几秒钟后再试，而在过载开始 5 分钟后被拒绝的客户端则会被要求等待更长时间。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The value is capped by `quarkus.load-shedding.max-retry-after` (120 seconds "
"by default) and is never shorter than 1 second, which is the granularity of "
"the header.\n"
"It is also jittered, so that clients rejected in the same instant are not "
"advised to come back in the same instant."
msgstr ""
"该值的上限由 `quarkus.load-shedding.max-retry-after` 决定（默认值为 120 秒），且绝不会短于 1 "
"秒——这是该标头的粒度。此外，该值还会进行抖动处理，以确保在同一时刻被拒绝的客户端不会被建议在同一时刻再次尝试连接。"

